{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1mdMyzxogeKiVjC8awu", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm stopping before sign-off. The device connection failed partway through the sweep, and every device call since then has returned `BrokenPipeError`, including `observe`, `screenshot`, `open_app` and `HOME`. I have not filed any reports, because I haven't confirmed a bug.\n\n**What I checked, with no defect found:**\n- **Deck list arrows:** Before a subdeck existed, no arrows showed. After I created `Spanish::Verbs`, an arrow appeared only on Spanish, not French, and the child deck had none. Expand and collapse worked, and the collapsed state survived a rotation to landscape and back.\n- **Tag dialog refresh:** A tag created in the dialog (`ser`) was listed the next time the dialog opened. A second tag (`animal`) created in the dialog also appeared when I reopened it from another note.\n- **Tag dialog cancel:** Ticking a tag and pressing Cancel left the note's tags unchanged.\n- **Add-note deck chooser:** From the browser, the initial deck followed the deck list's current selection: Spanish, then Spanish::Verbs, then French. Choosing a deck and changing it worked, and collapsing the chooser's tree worked. Adding a note with French as the deck put it in French, and the deck list counts updated (French 5, Spanish 4).\n- **Duplicate warning:** Typing `pain` in Front, where `pain` already exists in the note type, showed the red duplicate highlight.\n- **Edit note:** Changing Back to \"table furniture\" and adding the `verb` tag saved, and both changes persisted on the next search.\n\n**Unverified when the connection dropped:** Whether `animal` was actually applied to `gato` when I pressed Confirm. I was about to check this on the next screen, which would show whether the tag dialog's Confirm applies a newly created tag to the selected notes.\n\n**Test data I changed, to clean up if you want the collection back to its starting state:**\n- Added two French notes: `gato` (back `cat`) and `hat`.\n- Added the `verb` tag to `agua`, `gato` and `mesa`. `mesa`'s Back is now \"table furniture\".\n- Created the deck `Spanish::Verbs`.\n- Created the tags `ser` and `animal`. `animal` may be attached to `gato`.\n\n**Not covered:** the settings that affect notes, the rest of the card browser (sorting, flagging, suspend, delete), and rotation while the card editor is open.\n\n**Also noticed:** pressing Back on the root deck list closes the app. I did this twice by accident, so I've been relaunching with `open_app`.\n\nIf you restore the device connection, I'll confirm the `animal` tag result, cover the remaining areas, then file or sign off."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 149, "cache_read_input_tokens": 354722, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 149}, "output_tokens": 10, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "303ef245-97b4-4709-b966-d505f4df43d6", "uuid": "a9434201-e063-4877-9950-591aaaefa3d7", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T23:09:41.971Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1mdMj8NJ8zNoDoEd8e9"}
